Freeciv for RISC OS
===================

Freeciv is a free empire-building strategy game inspired by the history of
human civilisation: build cities, research technologies, trade, make war
and diplomacy, from the stone age to the space age. This is Freeciv 3.2.6
with its SDL2 client, and the server to play against the computer.

Web site: https://www.freeciv.org/

Requirements
------------
- RISC OS 5 on an ARMv7 machine (Raspberry Pi 2/3/4/5, BeagleBoard, ...).
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16+ and ARMEABISupport (from PackMan).
- About 80MB of free memory for a small game against the computer.
- For sound: SharedSound (part of RISC OS), and StreamManager and
  SharedSoundBuffer, in ssb.zip from
  https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html (merge its !System).
  John Duffell's own site (now on the Internet Archive) has more details:
  https://web.archive.org/web/20110920080106/http://www.duffell.riscos.me.uk/
  Without them the game is silent.

Playing
-------
Double-click !Freeciv. Choose "Start new game" to play against the
computer: the game starts its server in a TaskWindow ("Freeciv server" in
the Task Manager), which closes when you leave the game. The desktop keeps
running while you play.

You can also start the server yourself first, as with earlier RISC OS
versions of Freeciv: double-click !CivServer (a window shows the server's
messages and takes server commands), then !Freeciv, and choose "Start new
game". The client plays on the running server. Use this if the game can't
start a server by itself.

Client options, saved games and any extra data (tilesets, rulesets) go in
<Choices$Write>.Freeciv. Saved games are in <Choices$Write>.Freeciv.saves.

Notes and limits
----------------
- The game plays in a window (1024x768 to start with; change the size
  under Options > Local options > Interface > Screen resolution; it
  changes at once).
- Full screen (Options > Local options > Interface > Fullscreen) is a
  "full window", as in RDPClient: a window without borders that covers
  the screen. The desktop keeps running, so the server and other tasks
  carry on. Move the pointer to the bottom of the screen for the icon
  bar; click on the game to bring it back to the front. Turn the option
  off to go back to the window.
- The mouse wheel scrolls the map (with Shift: left and right) and the
  lists in dialogs.
- Music has two switches under Options > Local options > Sound: "Enable
  menu music" (before a game) and "Enable in-game music". Each only
  affects its own music, and stopping fades out over 2 seconds.
- English only in this build.
- The server list from the Internet (metaserver) and modpack downloads
  need https, which this build doesn't have yet. You can still connect to
  a server by name.
- If something goes wrong, turn on logging (see !Run) and look at
  <Wimp$ScrapDir>.FreecivLog and FreecivSrvLog.

